      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — removing unused imports/constants, and adding clear comments that describe the stream state at each step.Now I'll write the improved test file.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were:\n\n- **Removed unused imports** (`EOFException`, `assertFalse`, `assertNotNull`, `assertThrows`, `assertTrue`, `InputStream`, `ParameterizedTest`, `MethodSource`, `StringUtils`) — only `assertEquals` and `IOException` are needed.\n- **Removed the unused `MARK_RESET_NOT_SUPPORTED` constant** — it was never referenced in this test.\n- **Added a Javadoc on `TestNullInputStream`** explaining how `processByte()` maps stream position to byte values, which makes the read assertions (`assertEquals(0, ...)`, `assertEquals(7, ...)`) immediately interpretable.\n- **Added a Javadoc on `testSkip()`** with a numbered scenario showing the stream position after each operation — readers can follow the full 10-byte stream lifecycle without mentally simulating the state themselves.\n- **Improved inline comments** to state the stream position before each call and clarify *why* skip returns 2 (only 2 bytes remained) and why the last skip also returns -1 (EOF is idempotent). The last assertion's message was also updated from the duplicate `\"Skip 3 (EOF)\"` to `\"Skip 4 (EOF again)\"` to avoid confusion."
    }
